1
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:06,601
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:07,343 --> 00:00:08,610
Eh, what am I thinking?

3
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:11,301
I can't die here. I'll get 
hungry.

4
00:00:11,301 --> 00:00:13,754
I'll wander around some more and
if it gets really bad,

5
00:00:13,754 --> 00:00:16,738
I'll use one of those grenades 
to blow a hole in the building.

6
00:00:16,738 --> 00:00:18,707
It'll take out this vent, at 
least.

7
00:00:18,707 --> 00:00:20,059
Oh, I know where I am.

8
00:00:20,059 --> 00:00:22,767
I'm above the concrete corridor.
That clears things up.

9
00:00:23,742 --> 00:00:25,026
Rrrr!

10
00:00:25,026 --> 00:00:28,205
This sucks! An alligator could 
bite through this.

11
00:00:28,205 --> 00:00:31,848
I wonder if I bought a baby 
alligator and fed it and gave it
water,

12
00:00:31,848 --> 00:00:34,044
how long could it survive in 
these air ducts.

13
00:00:34,044 --> 00:00:35,458
That would be a good experiment.

14
00:00:35,458 --> 00:00:38,004
I'll try that at the next place 
I work at.

15
00:00:38,004 --> 00:00:39,770
I'm lost again.

16
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:42,148
Guess I'll go this way...

17
00:00:42,148 --> 00:00:44,579
Uh-oh! Blood. Better get ready.

18
00:00:44,579 --> 00:00:46,016
[gasp] The shotgun!

19
00:00:46,016 --> 00:00:46,467
SCIENTIST: Well...

20
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:47,886
SCIENTIST: so much for the 
government.
Wuh! How did you get in here?!

21
00:00:47,886 --> 00:00:51,634
SCIENTIST: Their idea of 
containment is to kill everyone 
associated with the project.

22
00:00:52,315 --> 00:00:54,026
SCIENTIST: Judging from your 
hazard suit
What...?

23
00:00:54,026 --> 00:00:55,403
SCIENTIST: you were part of what
went wrong.

24
00:00:55,403 --> 00:00:56,780
What the hell is that supposed 
to mean?

25
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:58,912
SCIENTIST: Now, look. If anyone 
can end this catastrophe,

26
00:00:58,912 --> 00:01:01,003
SCIENTIST: it's the Science Team
in the Lambda Complex

27
00:01:01,003 --> 00:01:02,761
SCIENTIST: at the opposite end 
of the base.

28
00:01:02,761 --> 00:01:05,889
SCIENTIST: With the transit 
system out, I couldn't tell you 
how to get there.

29
00:01:05,889 --> 00:01:08,105
SCIENTIST: But, there's an old 
decommissioned rail system

30
00:01:08,105 --> 00:01:09,213
SCIENTIST: somewhere through 
here.

31
00:01:09,213 --> 00:01:11,040
I don't care about any of this.

32
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,269
SCIENTIST: If you can make it 
through the rocket test labs,

33
00:01:13,269 --> 00:01:16,273
SCIENTIST: you might be able to 
worm your way through the old 
tunnels

34
00:01:16,273 --> 00:01:18,765
SCIENTIST: to track down what is
left of the Lambda Team.

35
00:01:18,765 --> 00:01:19,366
WHY?!

36
00:01:19,366 --> 00:01:21,697
SCIENTIST: You can trust them.  
You can trust all of us.

37
00:01:21,697 --> 00:01:23,247
I don't trust you at all.

38
00:01:23,247 --> 00:01:26,057
You appeared here like some 
magical genie out of a lamp.

39
00:01:26,057 --> 00:01:27,183
I don't understand why--

40
00:01:27,183 --> 00:01:27,926
SCIENTIST: I hear something!

41
00:01:27,926 --> 00:01:29,267
What? Where?

42
00:01:30,347 --> 00:01:31,534
There's nothing here.

43
00:01:33,041 --> 00:01:34,076
You're crazy.

44
00:01:34,076 --> 00:01:35,907
You're just like everyone else 
here.

45
00:01:35,907 --> 00:01:37,661
And where did that security 
guard go?

46
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:38,659
I didn't see him.

47
00:01:38,659 --> 00:01:42,934
He's off playing with that alien
in this giant funhouse of a 
ventilation system.

48
00:01:42,934 --> 00:01:45,210
At least this shotgun won't 
deceive me.

49
00:01:45,210 --> 00:01:48,315
It's filled with pellets, not 
lies.

50
00:01:48,315 --> 00:01:50,025
SCIENTIST: Do you know who ate 
all the doughnuts?

51
00:01:50,025 --> 00:01:50,533
NO!

52
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:53,463
Do you know if leptons are 
really compound particles?

53
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:54,368
Friggin' doughnuts...

54
00:01:54,368 --> 00:01:55,125
[button beeps]
Friggin' doughnuts...

55
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:55,500
Beep.

56
00:01:56,064 --> 00:01:58,886
Oh. This must be what that guy 
was screaming about.

57
00:01:58,886 --> 00:02:00,873
He would've wanted me to press 
that button.

58
00:02:00,873 --> 00:02:03,064
Hey, you're not really a genie, 
are you?

59
00:02:03,064 --> 00:02:04,562
You're not dressed like one.

60
00:02:04,562 --> 00:02:08,425
I asked because earlier I wished
for a shotgun and now I have a 
shotgun.

61
00:02:08,425 --> 00:02:10,285
But if that was one of my three 
wishes, I don't want to waste--

62
00:02:10,285 --> 00:02:12,372
[shotgun blast]
God! Sorry! Sorry...

63
00:02:12,372 --> 00:02:13,927
I-I'll just go, okay?

64
00:02:13,927 --> 00:02:14,640
I'm going.

65
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:15,381
Sorry...

66
00:02:15,381 --> 00:02:16,151
God...

67
00:02:16,151 --> 00:02:18,795
Well, I can forget about my 
other two wishes now.

68
00:02:18,795 --> 00:02:20,956
I'm never going to own a water 
park.

69
00:02:20,956 --> 00:02:21,922
Ah well.

70
00:02:21,922 --> 00:02:23,667
I don't think he was a genie 
anyway.

71
00:02:24,209 --> 00:02:26,349
You can't trust anyone.

72
00:02:26,349 --> 00:02:27,041
Ah hah!

73
00:02:27,041 --> 00:02:29,667
[bullsquid spitting]
Wood is not bullet proof.

74
00:02:29,667 --> 00:02:33,801
[bullsquid spitting, shotgun 
blasts]

75
00:02:33,801 --> 00:02:34,631
[bullsquid spitting]
Yeah.

76
00:02:34,631 --> 00:02:36,046
[bullsquid spitting]
See, the quality of my life

77
00:02:36,046 --> 00:02:37,962
[bullsquid spitting]
is going straight up now that I 
have

78
00:02:37,962 --> 00:02:39,018
[bullsquid spitting]
a shotgun.

79
00:02:39,018 --> 00:02:40,260
[bullsquid spitting]
I knew this would happen.

80
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,555
[bullsquid spitting]

81
00:02:41,555 --> 00:02:42,990
[bullsquid spitting]
What the hell is that noise?

82
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:43,947
[bullsquid spitting]

83
00:02:43,947 --> 00:02:45,592
[bullsquid spitting]
It sounds like somebody is 
frying bacon

84
00:02:45,592 --> 00:02:47,342
[bullsquid spitting]
and smacking their head against 
the pan.

85
00:02:47,342 --> 00:02:48,432
[bullsquid spitting]

86
00:02:48,432 --> 00:02:49,749
[bullsquid spitting]
Will you cut that out?

87
00:02:49,749 --> 00:02:51,348
[bullsquid spitting]

88
00:02:51,348 --> 00:02:52,821
[bullsquid spitting]
Oh, it's not you.

89
00:02:52,821 --> 00:02:54,021
[bullsquid spitting]

90
00:02:54,021 --> 00:02:55,352
[bullsquid spitting]
It's you!

91
00:02:55,352 --> 00:02:56,334
[bullsquid spitting]
But, you're closer.

92
00:02:58,233 --> 00:02:59,133
Oh, did he stop?

93
00:02:59,353 --> 00:03:00,570
[bullsquid spitting]
Nope.

94
00:03:00,570 --> 00:03:01,834
[bullsquid spitting]
Cthulhu dog...

95
00:03:02,248 --> 00:03:04,612
[bullsquid spitting]
Y'know, Cthulhu is supposed to 
be really big.

96
00:03:04,612 --> 00:03:06,534
[bullsquid spitting]
Frankly, I'm quite disappointed.

97
00:03:07,158 --> 00:03:09,209
So, what was that guy saying was
happening?

98
00:03:09,209 --> 00:03:11,278
That this is a military coverup?

99
00:03:11,278 --> 00:03:12,606
What is he smoking?

100
00:03:12,606 --> 00:03:15,178
Does he realize how impractical 
that would be?

101
00:03:15,178 --> 00:03:16,959
This facility's huge!

102
00:03:16,959 --> 00:03:19,440
We must hire almost a thousand 
people.

103
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,288
You can't track down every 
single--

104
00:03:21,288 --> 00:03:22,618
[banging]

105
00:03:23,574 --> 00:03:24,779
And aliens!

106
00:03:24,779 --> 00:03:27,386
We've got aliens popping up out 
of nowhere.

107
00:03:27,386 --> 00:03:29,293
Think people won't notice that?

108
00:03:29,293 --> 00:03:32,106
What are they going to do, say 
they're all mutant prairie dogs?

109
00:03:32,106 --> 00:03:33,767
Shoot everyone in New Mexico?

110
00:03:34,166 --> 00:03:35,567
Hey, a grenade!

111
00:03:35,567 --> 00:03:37,300
Well, I'll take one more.

112
00:03:38,662 --> 00:03:40,500
"Explosives".

113
00:03:41,798 --> 00:03:44,967
Whoa! That is a lot of 
explosives.

114
00:03:44,967 --> 00:03:46,846
And that is, what, an oxygen 
tank?

115
00:03:46,846 --> 00:03:48,340
Boy, if I dropped a grenade 
here,

116
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,990
I might be able to make my own 
exit out of this building.

117
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:53,040
But, I'd probably just die, 
so...

118
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,350
[clicking sound, klaxons sound]

119
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:55,576
[klaxons sound]
So, what did that do?

120
00:03:55,576 --> 00:03:56,739
[klaxons sound]

121
00:03:56,739 --> 00:03:57,988
[klaxons sound]
Beep beep beep.

122
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:00,013
[klaxons sound]
It's the same old story.

123
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:02,139
[klaxons sound]

124
00:04:02,139 --> 00:04:05,638
[klaxons sound]
Oh no. Not down again.

125
00:04:05,638 --> 00:04:07,944
Well, I like how at least the 
lights are red.

126
00:04:07,944 --> 00:04:10,794
It's letting me know ahead of 
time I'm descending into Hell.

127
00:04:10,794 --> 00:04:13,809
This whole facility's designed 
to keep me down.

128
00:04:13,809 --> 00:04:15,834
Gravity is so biased.

129
00:04:16,235 --> 00:04:22,592
[hums song]

130
00:04:22,592 --> 00:04:24,240
I don't see a vent.

131
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:27,148
The building better not start 
dropping facehuggers on me 
again;

132
00:04:27,148 --> 00:04:29,234
that was really uncalled for 
last time.

133
00:04:30,132 --> 00:04:31,202
Work it.

134
00:04:31,202 --> 00:04:33,815
Whoa! This one drops fast!

135
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:37,847
I bet if I jumped now, I'd break
my legs landing trying to catch 
up with it.

136
00:04:37,847 --> 00:04:40,965
When I build a house, I want an 
elevator just like this.

137
00:04:40,965 --> 00:04:43,400
The servants can use the stairs.

138
00:04:45,648 --> 00:04:47,065
Don't look at me.

139
00:04:47,065 --> 00:04:50,356
You're not worthy and it's 
better you learned your place in
life.

140
00:04:51,522 --> 00:04:53,100
What is this, a train track?

141
00:04:54,008 --> 00:04:54,667
Car?

142
00:04:55,209 --> 00:04:56,367
Does this work?

143
00:04:59,389 --> 00:05:00,819
Hey!

144
00:05:00,819 --> 00:05:01,686
This is great!

145
00:05:01,686 --> 00:05:02,267
[houndeye charges up]

146
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:03,974
No, no, NO!

147
00:05:03,974 --> 00:05:06,012
God, why does this always 
happen?

148
00:05:06,012 --> 00:05:09,968
Whenever I'm having a good time,
somebody has to go out of their 
way to ruin it!

149
00:05:11,662 --> 00:05:15,267
This is the same crap conductors
had to go through in the 1800s!

150
00:05:15,859 --> 00:05:17,067
NOTHING CHANGES!

151
00:05:17,815 --> 00:05:21,667
I understand I have to fight for
what's mine, but why is it ALL 
THE TIME?!

152
00:05:22,230 --> 00:05:23,400
How do I stop this?

153
00:05:25,317 --> 00:05:26,000
No...!

154
00:05:27,638 --> 00:05:28,231
[alarm buzzes]
Bad...!

155
00:05:28,231 --> 00:05:29,025
[alarm buzzes]

156
00:05:29,025 --> 00:05:30,990
[alarm buzzes]
Stop beeping at me!

157
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:32,477
[alarm buzzes]
This is all your fault!

158
00:05:32,477 --> 00:05:34,452
[alarm buzzes]

159
00:05:34,452 --> 00:05:36,598
[alarm buzzes]
You're a bunch of Mexican 
jumping beans!

160
00:05:36,598 --> 00:05:38,106
[alarm buzzes]

161
00:05:38,106 --> 00:05:40,868
[alarm buzzes]
Beep beep beep beep beep beep 
beep beep

162
00:05:41,039 --> 00:05:43,712
[alarm buzzes]
beep beep beep beep beep beep 
beep beep

163
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,555
[alarm buzzes]
beep beep beep beep beep--

164
00:05:45,555 --> 00:05:47,526
Yeah, I'm going to go crazy 
doing that.

165
00:05:47,526 --> 00:05:50,067
This must be why the railway 
industry died off.

166
00:05:50,737 --> 00:05:53,400
They would always crash into 
ponds of green...

167
00:05:53,947 --> 00:05:55,133
radioactive...

168
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:56,420
crap...

169
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,543
[Geiger counter clicks]
What?

170
00:05:58,543 --> 00:06:01,629
[Geiger counter clicks]
Ah, a radioactive spill.

171
00:06:01,629 --> 00:06:03,509
[Geiger counter clicks]
Part of me wants to believe 
we're not

172
00:06:03,509 --> 00:06:05,759
[Geiger counter clicks]
THIS criminally incompetent,

173
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:07,928
[Geiger counter clicks]
but I know better.

174
00:06:07,928 --> 00:06:10,144
[Geiger counter clicks]
Oh, man, listen to that...

175
00:06:10,144 --> 00:06:12,297
[Geiger counter clicks]

176
00:06:12,297 --> 00:06:14,496
[Geiger counter clicks]
I don't want to go this way...

177
00:06:14,496 --> 00:06:16,626
[Geiger counter clicks]

178
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,787
[Geiger counter clicks]
I better get a checkup after 
this...

179
00:06:18,787 --> 00:06:22,934
[Geiger counter clicks]

